### Test the API from VS Code
### Install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above each block.
### (Thunder Client or Postman work too: copy the method, URL and body.)

### Is the server running?
GET http://localhost:3000/

### All shows in My List
GET http://localhost:3000/api/mylist

### Add a show -> 201
POST http://localhost:3000/api/mylist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 169,
  "name": "Breaking Bad",
  "image": null,
  "genres": ["Drama", "Crime", "Thriller"],
  "rating": 9.2
}

### Add a second show (only id and name are required) -> 201
POST http://localhost:3000/api/mylist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 431,
  "name": "Friends"
}

### Same show again -> 409
POST http://localhost:3000/api/mylist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 169,
  "name": "Breaking Bad"
}

### Missing name -> 400
POST http://localhost:3000/api/mylist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 169
}

### id is text, not a number -> 400
POST http://localhost:3000/api/mylist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "169",
  "name": "Breaking Bad"
}

### Broken JSON (look at the comma at the end) -> 400
POST http://localhost:3000/api/mylist
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 169,
  "name": "Breaking Bad",
}

### One show
GET http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/169

### A show that is not in the list -> 404
GET http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/999999

### Update status, my rating and note (stretch) -> 200
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/169
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "watching",
  "myRating": 5,
  "note": "Up to season 3"
}

### Clear my rating again (null is allowed) -> 200
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/169
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "myRating": null
}

### Bad status -> 400
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/169
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "finished"
}

### myRating must be 1 to 5 -> 400
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/169
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "myRating": 7
}

### PATCH a show that is not in the list -> 404
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/999999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "watched"
}

### Delete -> 204
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/169

### Delete again -> 404
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/mylist/169

### A route that doesn't exist -> 404
GET http://localhost:3000/api/nothing-here
